Review the most recent earnings reports and economic forecasts, prioritizing the reports of the largest companies in the S&P 500 and forecasts from reputable sources like the Federal Reserve and IMF. Determine if aggregate earnings are generally exceeding or falling short of expectations, and if the economic outlook is generally optimistic or pessimistic. Align your sentiment accordingly: positive earnings and optimistic outlook suggest bullish sentiment, while negative earnings and a pessimistic outlook suggest bearish sentiment. Adjust your conviction based on the consistency and reliability of the information.